      "content": "That sounds like it could work, but we have to be careful. If the press digs into the archives and sees that the bill he voted against was actually the main funding bill and not some \"different version,\" we're dead. We'll look like we're lying straight to their faces. \n\nBut if we just admit he voted no on the community center bill, our favorability is shot. Seriously, give me the most effective line. Should we just tell them he was voting against a specific, flawed clause in it to make it seem like he was actually trying to protect the fund's long-term stability? Even if that specific clause wasn't the main reason? I need something we can stick to confidently.",
